# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# QMULATE — environment template. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
# NEVER commit a real `.env`. Secrets live in the Railway secret store (NFR-06).
# Every variable here is validated by `@qmulate/config` (zod, fail-fast).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# RESIDENCY GUARDRAIL — NFR-03 / release gate G-8. READ THIS.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# QMULATE handles real Saudi family-waqf data: beneficiary identities, IBANs,
# deed numbers, UBO records. That data is subject to KSA data residency and the
# PDPL, and it MUST NOT leave KSA-resident infrastructure.
#
# Until a KSA-resident production environment exists, the ONLY legal value of
# DATA_CLASSIFICATION anywhere — local, CI, Railway staging — is `fixture-only`.
#
#   fixture-only : the process may only ever touch invented data, i.e.
#                  `data/fixtures/sample-waqf.json`. The seed refuses to run on
#                  any other input file, and refuses to run at all unless this
#                  flag is exactly `fixture-only`.
#   production   : reserved. Legal ONLY on KSA-resident infrastructure that has
#                  passed the residency review. Setting it anywhere else is a
#                  G-8 violation and CI is wired to fail on it.
#
# There is deliberately NO `SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION` escape hatch: the app refuses
# to boot when DATA_CLASSIFICATION is missing or invalid.
DATA_CLASSIFICATION=fixture-only

# ── Database — FOUR CONNECTIONS, THREE ROLES  (ADR-0008 round 6) ─────────────
#
# Privilege separation is a DEPLOYMENT control, not only a schema one. The runtime
# connects as a role that CANNOT write the authorization plane and CANNOT run DDL;
# the credentials that can are separate, and two of them must not exist in an
# application service's environment at all.
#
# Create the roles once per environment, on the platform superuser:
#   pnpm exec tsx scripts/provision-db-roles.ts
#
# ── DATABASE_URL — the LEAST-PRIVILEGE RUNTIME ROLE (required) ───────────────
# Must be a postgres:// or postgresql:// URL, and must connect as `qmulate_app`:
#   · SELECT-only on `waqf_access_grant` and `membership` (no INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE)
#   · owns no table, so no `ALTER TABLE … DISABLE TRIGGER`, no `DROP TRIGGER`
#   · cannot `SET session_replication_role = 'replica'` (needs superuser)
#
# ⚠ A URL WHOSE ROLE OWNS THE SCHEMA SILENTLY DISABLES MIGRATIONS 10 AND 11.
# GRANTs and `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` both yield to the table owner, so the app
# would keep working while every control was decorative — which is precisely the
# state this repository was in for all of Sprint 2. `packages/database`'s
# authorization-plane integration test FAILS (never skips) when the posture is
# absent; it is the only thing that notices.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://qmulate_app:qmulate@localhost:5432/qmulate_dev?schema=public

# ── ACCESS_MATRIX_DATABASE_URL — the only credential that may mint a seat OR DECIDE
#    AN APPROVAL (the authority plane) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Connects as `qmulate_provisioner`. INSERT/UPDATE on `waqf_access_grant` and
# `membership`, UPDATE on `approval_request` (S12-1 / AV4-02, migration 50 — it
# DECIDES a request, never MINTS one), INSERT on `audit_event`, SELECT elsewhere —
# and nothing else. It owns nothing, so `waqf_access_grant_admission` and the
# `approval_request_authority` trigger are FULLY LIVE on it. Narrower, not exempt.
#
# Needed by any service that serves `grant.activate` or ANY approve procedure
# (`approval.approve`, `reservedMatter.approve`, `settings.set`,
# `endowment.recordDeedTerms`). Optional: a service without it fails CLOSED (the
# provisioning and decision functions throw, naming this variable) rather than
# falling back to DATABASE_URL.
ACCESS_MATRIX_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://qmulate_provisioner:qmulate@localhost:5432/qmulate_dev?schema=public

# ── MIGRATOR_DATABASE_URL — migrations, seed and test scaffolding ONLY ───────
# ⚠ MUST NOT BE PRESENT IN THE WEB OR WORKER SERVICE ENVIRONMENT.
# Connects as `qmulate_owner`, which OWNS every table — so it can suspend every
# guard trigger in migrations 1–11 and write the authorization plane directly. It
# is the credential for `prisma migrate deploy`, `db:seed`, the integration
# harnesses' scaffolding, and the one-off bootstrap of an endowment's first admin
# seat. `apps/web` and `apps/worker` call `assertNoPrivilegedDatabaseUrls()` at
# boot and REFUSE TO START if they find it.
MIGRATOR_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://qmulate_owner:qmulate@localhost:5432/qmulate_dev?schema=public

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PROVISIONING ONLY — NEVER AN APPLICATION SERVICE
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SUPERUSER_DATABASE_URL is the PLATFORM credential (Railway's `postgres`, CI's
# service-container superuser, the embedded cluster's `qmulate`). A superuser
# bypasses GRANTs, ownership checks AND `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`, so every
# "it is blocked" result obtained on it is worthless. Used by exactly one command
# — `scripts/provision-db-roles.ts` — once per environment.
SUPERUSER_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://qmulate:qmulate@localhost:5432/qmulate_dev?schema=public

# ── PGBOSS_DATABASE_URL — the queue transport's OWN credential (S10/T1) ──────
# Connects as `qmulate_pgboss`, which OWNS schema `pgboss` and holds NOTHING in
# `public` — it cannot read endowment data or touch the authorization plane.
# WORKER-ONLY: apps/worker needs it; apps/web REFUSES TO BOOT while holding it
# (assertNoWorkerOnlyDatabaseUrls). Not on the privileged list — see the written
# reasoning in packages/config/src/privileged-urls.ts — but not harmless either:
# a holder can drop or drain the queue schema and silently stop the deadline
# engine, so treat it as a service credential, never a shared convenience.
PGBOSS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://qmulate_pgboss:qmulate@localhost:5432/qmulate_dev?schema=public
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Auth — better-auth, self-hosted (required) ───────────────────────────────
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET must be at least 32 characters. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 48
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=replace-me-with-at-least-32-characters-of-random
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Extra browser origins allowed to call the auth API (comma-separated, scheme://host[:port], no
# wildcards). BETTER_AUTH_URL's own origin is always trusted. Local: the office-LAN address of this
# machine so http://<lan-ip>:3000 is the same app/database/users as localhost. Production: only a
# custom domain that fronts the same deployment. Leave unset otherwise.
# BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=http://192.168.0.101:3000

# Email second factor ("Email code" on the two-factor screen) and, later, verification mail. ALL
# FIVE are required for email delivery; with any of them unset the send-code endpoint answers
# 503 EMAIL_NOT_CONFIGURED and only the authenticator app / recovery codes work. Use an approved
# SMTP sender (STARTTLS on 587, or implicit TLS on 465); never commit credentials.
# Resend SMTP (verified sending domain app.qmulate.ai): host smtp.resend.com, port 465 (implicit
# TLS) or 587 (STARTTLS), username literally `resend`, password = a Resend API key with sending
# access. The same four settings serve local, LAN and production; only the key differs per env.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.resend.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# SMTP_USER=resend
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
# SMTP_FROM=Cumulate App <no-reply@app.qmulate.ai>

# ── Runtime (optional — defaults shown) ──────────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=info
PORT=3000

# Idle-session timeout in minutes for money-movement and statutory-filing roles.
# NFR-06 security target (30), NOT a statutory figure — but kept configurable
# rather than hardcoded so it can be tightened without a code change.
SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES=30

# ── Client-exposed (NEXT_PUBLIC_*, inlined into the browser bundle) ──────────
# Never put a secret behind a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Arabic is the product default, not a fallback.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_LOCALE=ar

# ── Field encryption — §12, application-level AES-256-GCM (required) ─────────
# UBO national-ID / IBAN / banking-reference columns are ciphertext even to a
# database operator with SELECT. Keys are VERSIONED so they can be rotated
# without downtime: add a new version, flip ACTIVE_KEY, re-encrypt in the
# background, then retire the old version.
#
# Generate a key with:  openssl rand -base64 32
# The HMAC key is deliberately SEPARATE from every encryption key — it backs the
# searchable equality lookup (e.g. dedupe an IBAN) so the app never decrypts to
# search. Compromising it must not reveal plaintext.
# The two values below decode to the ASCII strings "QMULATE-DEV-FIXTURE-ONLY-ENC-KEY" and
# "QMULATE-DEV-FIXTURE-ONLY-HMACKEY". They are placeholders for fixture-only environments —
# valid length, zero entropy, and obviously not secret. NEVER use them anywhere real.
FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEYS={"1":"UU1VTEFURS1ERVYtRklYVFVSRS1PTkxZLUVOQy1LRVk="}
FIELD_ENCRYPTION_ACTIVE_KEY=1
FIELD_HMAC_KEY=UU1VTEFURS1ERVYtRklYVFVSRS1PTkxZLUhNQUNLRVk=

# ── Seed / guardrail testing (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Overrides the seed's input file. The seed MUST reject anything that is not
# `data/fixtures/sample-waqf.json`; CI's residency-guardrail job proves it by
# asserting a non-zero exit when this points elsewhere.
# SEED_FILE=data/fixtures/sample-waqf.json

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ⚠ TEST-ONLY — RELAX THE AUTH RATE LIMITER. LEAVE THIS COMMENTED OUT.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# COMMENTED OUT ON PURPOSE, and un-commenting it in your `.env` is not the way
# to use it. `.env` is loaded by EVERY process in this repo (@qmulate/config's
# loadRootEnv), so a value here would relax the limiter for your dev server too
# — and `cp .env.example .env` is the documented first step, so a live line here
# would hand every developer a weakened control by default.
#
# WHAT IT IS. Since S7 the Playwright suite runs against `next build` +
# `next start`, because that is the only measured fix for the `next dev`
# memory-threshold restart that made seven consecutive CI E2E legs green only
# by retry. A production server ENFORCES better-auth's rate limiter — off in
# development, on in production — and the suite signs in ~74 times from one IP,
# so it collects `429 Too many requests`. better-auth's built-in `/sign-in*`
# rule is 3 requests per 10 seconds and no window/max setting widens it.
#
# HOW IT FAILS CLOSED (packages/auth/src/rate-limit.ts):
#   · absent / unset / empty        → FULL rate limiting. No exceptions.
#   · any other value              → the app REFUSES TO BOOT, naming the
#                                    variable. `false` is not "off".
#   · this token, but
#     DATA_CLASSIFICATION is not
#     `fixture-only`               → FULL rate limiting. TWO independent
#                                    conditions are required, because staging
#                                    is deliberately fixture-only and a
#                                    classification-only gate would disable the
#                                    limiter on a DEPLOYED environment.
#
# WHERE IT IS LEGITIMATELY SET. `.github/workflows/ci.yml`'s **e2e job only**,
# and on the local E2E command in BUILD-PLAN.md's "Run locally" block:
#
#   TEST_ONLY_DISABLE_AUTH_RATE_LIMIT=disabled-for-tests \
#     pnpm turbo run test:e2e
#
# Owner-approved: docs/product/prd/S4-owner-decision-memo.md, "S7 ·
# E2E-vs-rate-limiter posture" (2026-08-19).
# TEST_ONLY_DISABLE_AUTH_RATE_LIMIT=disabled-for-tests

# Supabase — used by @supabase/server in apps/web. Values come from the Supabase dashboard
# (Project Settings → API). SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY is server-only: never prefix it NEXT_PUBLIC_.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=
